      "contextFingerprint": "b7d93261fcfb9e18fcaa6f5d9e969ff22c5a5eb507be70c6a8dc97af0e9f0779",
      "sourceText": "`min_intensity=0.1` 把10 cm作为进入二维障碍轮廓的高差下限，不是说车辆能跨10 cm台阶。降低它可能看见更低障碍，也可能把正常地面或坡面误差画进地图；提高它会减少小高差轮廓，却可能漏掉对实车危险的低障碍。远场地形高差取绝对值，坡面较低一侧也可能过门槛；近场目前忽略负高差，4 m交接处的差异仍会传入扫描。",
      "translatedText": "`min_intensity=0.1`Using 10 cm as the lower limit for height difference when entering a two\\-dimensional obstacle contour does not mean that the vehicle can climb over a 10 cm step\\. Lowering it may reveal lower obstacles, but may also map normal ground or slope errors into the map; raising it will reduce contours with small height differences, but may miss low obstacles that are dangerous to the real vehicle\\. For far\\-field terrain, the absolute value of the height difference is taken, so the lower side of a slope may also cross the threshold; the near field currently ignores negative height differences, and the difference at the 4 m handover will still propagate into the scan\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 222,
        "outputTokens": 137,
        "costUsd": 0.000231
      }
    },
